            <ArticleTitle>Posterosuperior glenoid rim impingement as a cause of shoulder pain in top level waterpolo players.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>273-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To further define the impingement occurring between the undersurface of the rotator cuff and the posterosuperior glenoid rim as a cause of shoulder pain in waterpolo athletes.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="EXPERIMENTAL DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">A prospective design was used in the last three years.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">Data were collected in Science Sports Institute of Rome.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PARTICIPANTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Eleven top level waterpolo players of both sexes all members of Italian National Waterpolo teams complaining of shoulder pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">All the eleven cases were previously examined with clinical test and X-ray and MR imaging in conventional and functional views, and then underwent arthroscopy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In four cases, X-ray showed erosions of the posterosuperior glenoid and in 5 cases, osteochondral defects on the posterior aspect of humeral head. In eleven cases, MR detected posterosuperior labral damages, partial tears of the undersurface of the rotator cuff and posterosuperior glenoid impingement. Furthermore arthroscopy detected in all cases the pathological findings associated with the posterosuperior glenoid impingement.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Even if the shoulder pain in the overhead athlete may be multifactorial, this study provides further evidence that the posterosuperior glenoid impingement may be the major cause of shoulder pain in waterpolo athletes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
